<title>USA: Top manufacturing states - survey.</title>
<headline>Top manufacturing states - survey.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are states with the most major manufacturing companies in 1996, according to IndustryWeek magazine's IndustryWeek 1000 list, compiled with Dun &amp; Bradstreet Corp. and Moody's Investor Service.</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>California - 36 companies</p>
<p>New York - 30</p>
<p>Illinois - 29</p>
<p>Ohio - 25</p>
<p>Pennsylvania - 23</p>
<p>Texas - 22</p>
<p>Connecticut - 17</p>
<p>New Jersey - 17</p>
<p>Michigan - 13</p>
<p>Massachusetts - 10</p>
<p>Minnesota - 10</p>
<p>Missouri - 10</p>
<p>Georgia - 8</p>
<p>Virginia - 8</p>
<p>Indiana - 7</p>
<p>Wisconsin - 7</p>
<p>Colorado - 5</p>
<p>Maryland - 4</p>
<p>North Carolina - 4</p>
<p>Oregon - 4</p>
<p>Washington - 4</p>
